From 0fe735916f29db249c5f2cb0c069eea8ede21f57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:56:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dynarmic A32: constant offsets in fastmem accesses, float
 compare branches fused, no redundant extensions

What the translated code of compiled ARM C executes (callgrind, per instruction, harness): guest
register loads/stores 23-29%, LEAs 11-16% (2-7% an address for the next access), a float
compare-and-branch ~10% of a float-heavy program (ucomiss, then sete/rcl/shr/pext into the FPSCR's
and the CPSR's NZCV, sahf, jcc), a movzx after every LDRB/LDRH and before every STRB/STRH. Mario
Kart's hottest code: a third of its instructions are loads/stores at a register plus a constant.

- UserConfig::fold_address_offsets (Eden: on): A32EmitX64::FoldAddressOffsets, before a block is
  emitted: a plain (not ordered, not exclusive) fastmem load or store through Add32(base, 1..65535)
  used by it alone takes the base, the constant goes in its displacement ([r13 + base + disp]),
  the Add32 goes. A fault there fake-calls a per-access stub (push base; lea base32, [base + disp];
  call the fallback; pop; ret): the address whole, with the 32-bit wrap (one past 4 GiB faults in
  the PS4's 2^39 arena; negative offsets aren't folded, they could go below it). Where the access
  needs the address whole otherwise (no fastmem for it, ordered, the value in the base's register),
  the LEA as before.
- UserConfig::skip_redundant_extensions (Eden: on): a ZeroExtend of an A32ReadMemory8/16 is its
  value (every way of loading it zero-extends), an A32WriteMemory8/16 of LeastSignificantByte/Half
  (used by it alone) stores from the word's register.
- A float compare's flags (VCMP; VMRS APSR_nzcv, FPSCR; B<cond>): CondFlagsFP32/64 (ucomis of the
  operands, swapped for MI/PL/CS/CC/HI/LS so that every condition is one jump; EQ/NE look at the
  parity too). The look-ahead also tells whether the FPSCR's NZCV is dead at the exit (a VMRS reads
  it; VCMP, VMSR set it; calls and returns per abi): its stores go, and the FPCompare with them.

Host harness, valgrind's instruction count (04.04 -> this): game-like C 122,570 -> 107,047 a frame,
zlib 21.94M -> 20.04M a frame, Mario Kart's hottest loops 537 -> 469 an iteration. Old vs new: 5,000+
random A32 programs equal (gen/2/3/4/7/9/10, fastmem, split stack, a page past 4 GiB, marked and
unmapped pages, calls with and without the call standard), and zlib and the C benchmark at -O1,
-O2, -O3, -Os.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
